44bfdb88cd39066a25391","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":64,"end_line":68},"finding":null,"explanation":"The trigger keyword list is broad enough to match ordinary finance questions such as support/resistance, EMA, Fibonacci, or short-term trading. In a prompt-based skill system, this can cause unintended activation, making the assistant follow this trading framework when the user only wanted general discussion, which can override user intent and produce unsolicited trading instructions.","remediation":"Narrow activation rules to require stronger combinations of conditions, such as explicit opt-in phrases plus a market symbol and analysis intent. Add negative guards to avoid activation for general education/chat, and require confirmation before producing trade entries, stops, targets, or position-sizing recommendations.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":64,"end_line":68}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-8e245675a52f43ddbe90e8ef6eabd5b1","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.83,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":149},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill is written to operate in Chinese and requires a fixed report format without offering language negotiation or documenting a justified locale restriction. This can cause user misunderstanding, misexecution of financial instructions, or inaccessible risk disclosures when the user interacts in another language, which is especially problematic in a trading-advice context where clarity matters.","remediation":"Add explicit language negotiation at activation time, default to the user's language when possible, and only enforce Chinese when the user requests it or the deployment context documents that restriction. Ensure disclaimers, price levels, and risk instructions are available in the user's 